// New TypeScript 5 feature: Type-Only Equality Operators
// type hierarchy in typescript is based on structural typing, which means that two types are considered equal if they have the same structure, regardless of their names.

// any type is a top type in TypeScript, which means that it can be assigned to any other type without causing a type error.

